src/opencore/smbios.rs takes its serial number tables and rules from
OpenCorePkg's macserial (Copyright (c) 2018-2020 vit9696, Copyright (c) 2020
Matis Schotte), so that file is also under OpenCorePkg's BSD-3-Clause license:
LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-OpenCorePkg.txt.

What reims-util downloads and writes into images, such as OpenCore and OVMF,
is not part of the repository, and keeps its own license; OVMF's licenses are
written beside OVMF_CODE.fd. The crates the build takes from crates.io keep
their own licenses too.
